.Dd November 23, 2026
.Dt HMKTST 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm hmktst
.Nd run the usual hmarket storage and disk-count searches
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm hmktst
.Op Ar hmarket-flags ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a
.Xr sh 1
wrapper.
Run it from the repository directory.
It calls
.Pa ./hmarket
five times and prints a label before each table.
Extra arguments are appended to every call, which is how a snapshot is selected:
.Pp
.Dl ./hmktst -o jsonfile=data/27.json.xz
.Pp
The five searches, in order:
.Bl -tag -width "Storage min 40g price max 100" -compact
.It Storage min 40g price max 100
.Fl s Cm 40000
.Fl p Cm 100
.It Storage min 27g price max 80
.Fl s Cm 27000
.Fl p Cm 80
.It Disk count min 5 price max 80
.Fl c Cm 5
.Fl p Cm 80
.It Lotta disk cheap
.Fl s Cm 80000
.It Lucky draw: 7 disk min
.Fl c Cm 7
.El
.Pp
.Fl s
is gigabytes after
.Xr hmarket 1
parses the snapshot.
A 40 TB disk is 40000 in that unit because a
.Ql TB
size is multiplied by 1000.
ECC and Enterprise HDD stay on, since this wrapper does not pass
.Fl e .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The exit status is the status of the last
.Xr hmarket 1
call.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr hmarket 1 ,
.Xr hmktvm 1 ,
.Xr update_data 1
